{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 120, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing the edge-0 avg_pool with a 1x1 conv gave +7 to +10 when edge 4 was skip_connect, versus under +4 for most other edge-4 ops."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "With edge 4 as avg_pool the edge-0 1x1 conv gain was +6.8/+11.9/+10.9, far above the cases where edge 4 was none or a conv."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 5 cost -5.4/-10.9/-13.9 when edge 0 was none, much more than with a conv on edge 0."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Dropping edge 5 hurt much more with a weak avg_pool on edge 0 (-3.8/-7.4/-11.6) than with nor_conv_3x3 there (-0.4/-2.0/-3.4)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 3 when edge 4 is already none cut the only remaining path and cost -2.5/-6.2/-11.2, the worst case among edge-3 removals."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Swapping the edge-5 avg_pool for a 1x1 conv gained +4.6/+5.7/+6.9 with edge 1 as skip_connect, versus about +0.5 to +3 with a conv."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "With edge 1 as avg_pool the edge-5 1x1 conv gain was about +5.6/+6.2/+6.4, larger than with conv or none on edge 1."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "The edge-5 3x3 conv gain was +7.0/+5.8/+7.9 with avg_pool on edge 0, versus about +1 to +6 with nor_conv_3x3 there."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op